# Inputs written to cover cases the Kotlin tests don't.
# Format and updating: see tests/parse.rs.

=== if else chains by call joins
if (a) { b } else if (c) { d } else { e }
--- tree
(CallJoin
  (Curly (Paren if "(" a ")") { b })
  callJoin:
  (CallJoin
    (Curly (Paren [else if] "(" c ")") { d })
    callJoin:
    (Curly else { e })))

=== leading comma, which crashes Kotlin
, x
--- tree
(Comma , x)

=== link reference definition then a line, which crashes Kotlin (markdown)
[i]:h
"
--- tree
(Root)
comment Semilit 0..7
comment SemilitParagraph 6..7

=== multi-quoted string closed in a later code block, which crashes Kotlin (markdown)
    """
a

    ""
--- tree
(QuotedGroup "\"\"\"" (Paren "\n" "(" ")") (QuotedGroup "\"" "\"" "\"\"\""))
bracket 15..15: Unclosed { open: "(", close: ")", line: 4 }
comment Semilit 8..11
comment SemilitParagraph 8..10

=== unbalanced scriptlet with a comment, which crashes Kotlin
"""
:{//
`
--- tree
(Paren
  (CurlyGroup { (QuotedGroup "\"\"\"" (Semi ; (CurlyGroup { })) "\"\"\"") })
  "("
  (QuotedGroup ` `)
  ")")
comment Line 6..9

=== unbalanced scriptlet then content, which crashes Kotlin
"""
:{
`
~
--- tree
(Paren
  (CurlyGroup { (QuotedGroup "\"\"\"" (Semi ; (CurlyGroup { })) "\"\"\"") })
  "("
  (QuotedGroup ` "\n~" `)
  ")")
